--- bool — boolean utility functions for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `bool` stdlib logic: `and`, `or`, `not`,
--- `xor`, `nand`, `nor`, `implies`, `eq`. The Rust bridge in
--- `plugin-lib-utils` loads this file via `include_str!`, evaluates it to
--- obtain a record of procs, and applies the requested field to the caller's
--- boolean argument(s).
---
--- Handl's native `&&` (and), `||` (or), `!` (not), `==` (eq), and `!=` (neq)
--- operators work directly on booleans, so no dependency modules are
--- required. These operators are eager (both operands are evaluated before
--- the op applies), matching the prior Rust `Function` impls (see ADR 0040
--- note: short-circuit `and`/`or` are not yet supported by the new
--- non-generic `Module`/`Function` traits).
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- bool.and — logical conjunction of two booleans.
--- bool.or — logical disjunction of two booleans.
--- bool.not — logical negation of a boolean.
--- bool.xor — exclusive-or of two booleans.
--- bool.nand — negated conjunction (not-and) of two booleans.
--- bool.nor — negated disjunction (not-or) of two booleans.
--- bool.implies — logical implication (a implies b).
--- bool.eq — test whether two booleans are equal.
cap "bool.and"
cap "bool.or"
cap "bool.not"
cap "bool.xor"
cap "bool.nand"
cap "bool.nor"
cap "bool.implies"
cap "bool.eq"
{
  and: [a, b] ~> a && b,
  or: [a, b] ~> a || b,
  not: a ~> !a,
  xor: [a, b] ~> a != b,
  nand: [a, b] ~> !(a && b),
  nor: [a, b] ~> !(a || b),
  implies: [a, b] ~> !a || b,
  eq: [a, b] ~> a == b
}
